.TH smi-pki-ca-create "1" "September 2026" "SMI Toolset" "SMI PKI Command"
.SH NAME
smi-pki-ca-create \- Create a Root CA, optionally the Intermediate CA too
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B smi-pki-ca-create
.I DIRECTORY
.I ROOT_DOMAIN
.RI [ WITH_INTERMEDIATE ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.PP
.B smi-pki-ca-create
creates the Root CA in the \fBca\fR subdirectory of \fIDIRECTORY\fR for the given
\fIROOT_DOMAIN\fR.
By default only the Root CA is created; pass \fIWITH_INTERMEDIATE\fR as
\fBtrue\fR, \fByes\fR or \fB1\fR to also create the Intermediate CA in the same run.
Anything else, including omitting it, creates the Root CA alone.
.PP
Subject information is loaded from \fBsubject.sh\fR in \fIDIRECTORY\fR if present, giving
the country, state, locality, organization, organizational unit and email of the certificates.
.PP
The Root CA is a 4096-bit key and a self-signed certificate with a descriptive Common Name
(\fBHAS Internal Root CA\fR, not a host name), marked \fBbasicConstraints=critical,CA:TRUE\fR with
\fBkeyCertSign,cRLSign\fR.
Files \fB\fIROOT_DOMAIN\fB.priv.key\fR, \fB.pub.key\fR, \fB.csr\fR, \fB.crt\fR.
.PP
The Intermediate CA, when requested, is a 4096-bit key and a certificate signed by the Root CA,
never self-signed, marked \fBbasicConstraints=critical,CA:TRUE,pathlen:0\fR with
\fBkeyCertSign,cRLSign\fR.
Files \fB\fIROOT_DOMAIN\fB.intermediate.priv.key\fR, \fB.intermediate.pub.key\fR,
\fB.intermediate.csr\fR, \fB.intermediate.crt\fR.
It can also be created on its own later with \fBsmi-pki-start-intermediate-ca\fR(1).
.PP
The full chain is Root CA \[->] Intermediate CA \[->] Server certificate. The Root CA signs only
the Intermediate CA; routine server certificates are signed by the Intermediate CA with
\fBsmi-pki-create-domain-cert\fR(1), which therefore requires the Intermediate CA to exist first.
Only the Root CA certificate need be installed into trust stores. Private keys are written with
mode \fB600\fR, so the Root CA private key can be kept protected and offline.
.SH ARGUMENTS
.TP
.I DIRECTORY
Where the \fBca\fR subdirectory and the subject file live.
.TP
.I ROOT_DOMAIN
The root domain, for example \fBhas.ee.gintra\fR, used to name the CA files.
.TP
.I WITH_INTERMEDIATE
\fBtrue\fR, \fByes\fR or \fB1\fR to also create the Intermediate CA. Default: create the Root CA only.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I DIRECTORY/subject.sh
Optional subject information sourced for the certificate distinguished names.
.TP
.I DIRECTORY/ca
Root CA and Intermediate CA keys, requests, certificates and extension files.
.SH AUTHOR
.PP
Command written by Imre Tabur.
.SH "REPORTING BUGS"
.PP
Report smi-pki-ca-create bugs to \fIinfo@setmy.info\fR
.SH "SEE ALSO"
.PP
